message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Sparse connectome controllers under a sparse delayed liquid-biopsy-style observer"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Can sparse connectome-style controllers designed under full or dense
  observation still meet their declared steering bounds when the only map is
  the sparse delayed liquid-biopsy-style partial observer of Thesis #20?
  On one two-clone toy they cannot. The frozen sparse controller of Thesis #6
  meets a predeclared certificate under full state and under a dense
  zero-order hold. The same controller, fed only the lagged, sparsely sampled,
  censored burden scalar of Thesis #20, fails separation, action tracking,
  duty, and input deviation. Burden bounds and a state-deviation bound still
  pass. Restoring the sensitive fraction at the sparse instants returns the
  noise-free certificate, so the failure is the missing composition channel.
  The scalar is not a ctDNA assay. Not a dose. No document DOI.
keywords:
  - sparse controller
  - partial observation
  - steering bounds
  - liquid-biopsy-style observer
  - certainty equivalence
  - connectome-style expansion
  - toy ODE
  - research-only
